    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers around high-efficiency matchups, headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Corbin Carroll** (74.41). **Vinnie Pasquantino** is our standout play; he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Max Scherzer (5.31 xERA), with the platoon advantage and a premium #3 spot driving his score deep into the elite tier. **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start despite the moderate skill of the opposing arm, as his speed profile consistently offsets the risks of facing a high-efficiency hold pitcher. Joining them in the strong tier are **Seiya Suzuki** (64.62) and **Isaac Paredes** (64.14). **Isaac Paredes** earns a massive boost from a 9% dynamic platoon edge, while **Seiya Suzuki** is set up for success by a slow pitcher delivery that signals a high-ceiling day for stolen base opportunities.\n\nThe optimizer faced a tight decision at the fringe of the starting rotation, ultimately benching **Zach McKinstry** (47.06) in favor of **Mickey Moniak** (48.95) and **Jose Caballero** (55.35). While **Zach McKinstry** offers steady production, his negative platoon adjustment against a right-handed pitcher like Legumina kept him just outside the threshold for a daily start. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno** and **Henry Bolte**; while both occupy premium lineup spots, their official placement remains subject to final manager confirmations. Investors should note that while **Griffin Conine** flashed high xwOBA metrics, his poor matchup against a left-handed starter left him well below our 40.0 scoring floor, keeping him securely on the bench to preserve our game caps.",
